00:42:27.910 --> 00:42:29.930
And it's been wonderful.
而且效果一直很棒。

904
00:42:29.930 --> 00:42:38.750
But what I need now is also a pencil with an eraser that never disappears or pops off or can be chewed off.
但我现在还需要一支铅笔，上面的橡皮擦永远不会消失、掉落，或者被咬掉。

905
00:42:38.990 --> 00:42:39.150
Right.
没错。

906
00:42:39.390 --> 00:42:41.930
So we've solved the one problem.
所以我们解决了一个问题。

907
00:42:42.230 --> 00:42:44.910
But now I'm looking for that other thing.
但现在我在找另一件东西。

908
00:42:44.910 --> 00:42:51.310
So I was really drooling over this just cup of beautiful pencils with erasers.
所以我当时真的对着那一杯漂亮的带橡皮擦的铅笔垂涎三尺。

909
00:42:51.650 --> 00:42:52.170
Pencils.
铅笔。

910
00:42:52.330 --> 00:42:54.070
I guess you know my life now.
我想你现在了解我的生活了。

911
00:42:54.230 --> 00:42:59.470
But I believe there's someone out there listening who can relate deeply.
但我相信在听节目的听众里，一定有人能感同身受。

912
00:43:00.450 --> 00:43:01.590
Yeah, I can relate.
是啊，我能感同身受。

913
00:43:01.750 --> 00:43:02.470
I'm right here.
我就在这儿呢。

914
00:43:02.810 --> 00:43:03.090
Okay.
好吧。

915
00:43:05.490 --> 00:43:06.790
You're looking at her.
你正看着她呢。

916
00:43:07.050 --> 00:43:07.270
Yeah.
是啊。

917
00:43:07.990 --> 00:43:12.170
Back at Athlete, you know, Daryl is really impressed by the offices.
回到Athlete公司，你知道，达里尔对办公室印象非常深刻。

918
00:43:12.170 --> 00:43:16.450
And Pam says, yeah, Jim, you kind of undersold this.
帕姆说，是啊，吉姆，你之前有点低估这里了。

919
00:43:16.610 --> 00:43:17.570
Made it sound dinky.
把它说得太寒酸了。

920
00:43:18.310 --> 00:43:18.450
Yeah.
是啊。

921
00:43:18.710 --> 00:43:20.670
Jim says, hey, listen, it's only a startup.
吉姆说，嘿，听着，这毕竟只是个初创公司。

922
00:43:20.670 --> 00:43:22.470
I haven't even gotten a paycheck yet.
我甚至还没领到过工资呢。

923
00:43:22.470 --> 00:43:24.530
I mean, these things go down all the time.
我是说，这种公司随时都可能倒闭。

924
00:43:24.990 --> 00:43:29.450
And that's when Daryl says, well, I'd like to go down on with it.
就在这时，达里尔说，好吧，我愿意和它一起沉沦。

925
00:43:29.910 --> 00:43:30.130
Yeah.
是啊。

926
00:43:30.430 --> 00:43:32.490
We got a fan catch from Janelle W.
我们收到了来自宾夕法尼亚州北安普顿的珍妮尔·W的粉丝发现。

927
00:43:32.670 --> 00:43:41.430
in Northampton, Pennsylvania, who said the look between Pam and Jim seems to imply that Jenna and John are breaking.
她说帕姆和吉姆之间的眼神交流似乎暗示珍娜和约翰在笑场。

928
00:43:41.430 --> 00:43:46.350
Was this a scripted line, or did Craig actually have a blooper that made it into the final cut?
这是剧本里的台词，还是克雷格真的笑场了却被剪进了最终成片？

929
00:43:47.210 --> 00:43:48.670
Janelle, this was scripted.
珍妮尔，这是剧本里的。

930
00:43:48.850 --> 00:43:49.030
Yep.
没错。

931
00:43:49.450 --> 00:43:52.230
Craig just delivered it so well.
克雷格演得太好了。

932
00:43:53.110 --> 00:43:53.990
So well.
演得太好了。

933
00:43:54.130 --> 00:43:54.430
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

934
00:43:54.970 --> 00:43:59.470
Back at Dunder Mifflin, Erin now has a big box of pins on her desk.
回到邓德·米夫林公司，艾琳的桌上现在有一大盒大头针。

935
00:43:59.630 --> 00:44:00.510
She did it.
她做到了。

936
00:44:00.670 --> 00:44:00.990
Yeah.
是啊。

937
00:44:01.290 --> 00:44:02.890
The delivery went amazing.
送货过程非常顺利。

938
00:44:03.630 --> 00:44:05.330
She's not going to unpack them then.
那她不打算把它们拆开吗？

939
00:44:05.650 --> 00:44:07.030
Or should she unpack them?
或者她应该拆开它们吗？

940
00:44:07.110 --> 00:44:09.910
She's not sure if she should be a busybody or a lazybones.
她不确定自己该做一个爱管闲事的人还是一个懒骨头。

941
00:44:09.910 --> 00:44:12.510
Her brain is ping-ponging with this question.
她的大脑正因为这个问题而左右摇摆。

942
00:44:13.050 --> 00:44:17.690
Also, she's never had espresso before, so she's really amped up.
另外，她以前从没喝过浓缩咖啡，所以她现在非常兴奋。

943
00:44:17.990 --> 00:44:20.650
Well, Ange, fan catch from Maura L.
好吧，安吉，来自纽约长岛的莫拉·L的粉丝发现。

944
00:44:20.770 --> 00:44:22.610
in Long Island, New York, who said,
她说，

945
00:44:22.750 --> 00:44:25.930
I've been waiting the whole podcast to make this catch.
我等了整期播客就为了指出这个发现。

946
00:44:26.450 --> 00:44:31.530
Erin says she's never had an espresso before, but Michael makes her an espresso in Café Disco.
艾琳说她以前从没喝过浓缩咖啡，但迈克尔在《咖啡迪斯科》那一集里给她做过一杯。

947
00:44:32.010 --> 00:44:33.630
Great catch, Maura.
很棒的发现，莫拉。

948
00:44:34.150 --> 00:44:34.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

949
00:44:34.630 --> 00:44:38.010
Well, you know, there was more to this pin delivery moment.
嗯，你知道，大头针送达的那个时刻还有更多内容。

950
00:44:38.270 --> 00:44:42.370
There was a whole scene where the pins are delivered by a delivery guy named Mike.
原本有一整场戏，大头针是由一个叫迈克的送货员送来的。

951
00:44:42.530 --> 00:44:46.610
It's really funny, and you can tell how caffeinated Erin is.
这真的很有趣，你能看出艾琳喝了多少咖啡。

952
00:44:46.870 --> 00:44:47.470
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

953
00:44:55.970 --> 00:44:56.430
Hello.
你好。

954
00:44:57.030 --> 00:44:57.690
I'm here, too.
我也在这儿。

955
00:44:57.690 --> 00:44:58.070
Is this pens?
这是笔吗？

956
00:44:58.310 --> 00:44:59.210
Is this the delivery of pens?
这是送来的笔吗？

957
00:45:00.450 --> 00:45:01.230
I don't know.
我不知道。

958
00:45:01.350 --> 00:45:02.170
I don't open the boxes.
我不拆箱子。

959
00:45:03.770 --> 00:45:04.470
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

960
00:45:04.730 --> 00:45:05.550
It is the pens.
真的是笔。

961
00:45:05.730 --> 00:45:06.350
It's the pens.
是笔。

962
00:45:06.610 --> 00:45:07.630
Mike, is it?
迈克，是吗？

963
00:45:07.790 --> 00:45:08.590
It's the pens, Mike.
是笔，迈克。

964
00:45:08.890 --> 00:45:09.650
We did it.
我们做到了。

965
00:45:10.050 --> 00:45:10.830
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

966
00:45:11.070 --> 00:45:11.430
Wait.
等等。

967
00:45:11.710 --> 00:45:12.690
I don't have any cash.
我身上没现金。

968
00:45:12.970 --> 00:45:13.710
How do I...
我该怎么……

969
00:45:13.710 --> 00:45:14.710
What do I...
我该做什么……

970
00:45:14.710 --> 00:45:15.610
It's okay.
没关系。

971
00:45:16.170 --> 00:45:17.190
It's all paid for.
都已经付过钱了。

972
00:45:17.750 --> 00:45:19.470
You mother f***ing lifesaver.
你真是个他妈的救星。

973
00:45:19.630 --> 00:45:22.090
Get your sweet ass out of here before I do something crazy.
快把你那迷人的屁股挪走，不然我真要干出什么疯狂的事了。

974
00:45:22.990 --> 00:45:23.450
Bye.
再见。

975
00:45:23.450 --> 00:45:33.620
This is, you mother f***ing lifesaver.
这真是，你他妈的真是个救星。

976
00:45:36.650 --> 00:45:38.030
This is crazy.
这太疯狂了。

977
00:45:38.030 --> 00:45:39.070
She did it.
她做到了。

978
00:45:39.250 --> 00:45:41.510
She accepted a delivery of a box.
她签收了一箱快递。

979
00:45:41.750 --> 00:45:47.050
There's a perfect storm happening for Erin, which is this delivery plus caffeine.
对艾琳来说，现在是完美的风暴，快递加上咖啡因。

980
00:45:47.390 --> 00:45:47.630
Yeah.
是啊。

981
00:45:47.890 --> 00:45:50.350
And it's just going to keep getting ratcheted up.
而且情况只会越来越激烈。

982
00:45:50.530 --> 00:45:52.610
I have to ask you a question, Angela.
安吉拉，我得问你个问题。

983
00:45:53.350 --> 00:45:56.890
If you were you, not if you were Erin, but if you were you,
如果你是你自己，不是艾琳，而是你，

984
00:45:57.710 --> 00:46:00.690
would you put the pins away or just accept the delivery?
你会把笔收好，还是只负责签收？

985
00:46:00.930 --> 00:46:02.770
Would you be a busybody or a lazybone?
你会选择多管闲事，还是偷懒？

986
00:46:02.890 --> 00:46:03.830
I'd be a busybody.
我会选择多管闲事。

987
00:46:04.050 --> 00:46:04.850
I'd put them away.
我会把它们收好。

988
00:46:04.870 --> 00:46:08.290
And then maybe you would come back and be like, that's not where I intended them.
然后你可能会回来跟我说，那不是我想要放的地方。

989
00:46:08.370 --> 00:46:10.950
And I would be like, oh, well, that's where the other ones were.
我会说，哦，好吧，之前的笔就是放在那儿的。

990
00:46:11.470 --> 00:46:11.790
Hmm.
嗯。

991
00:46:12.150 --> 00:46:13.550
I guess I'd have sass, too.
我想我也会变得很刻薄。

992
00:46:14.790 --> 00:46:16.390
You'd be a sassy busybody.
你会成为一个刻薄的多管闲事者。

993
00:46:16.530 --> 00:46:16.690
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

994
00:46:17.810 --> 00:46:18.890
I would be a lazybones.
我会选择偷懒。

995
00:46:19.290 --> 00:46:19.610
Lazybones.
偷懒。

996
00:46:19.730 --> 00:46:20.670
Just accept the delivery.
只负责签收快递。

997
00:46:21.070 --> 00:46:22.190
That's what I was asked to do.
那是要求我做的事。

998
00:46:22.250 --> 00:46:22.990
That's what I'm going to do.
我就会照做。

999
00:46:23.030 --> 00:46:25.090
And it's not because I don't like to go above and beyond,
这并不是因为我不喜欢超越自我，

1000
00:46:25.090 --> 00:46:28.970
but I assume other people might have their system.
而是我假设其他人可能有他们自己的系统。

1001
00:46:29.210 --> 00:46:31.450
And so I'm not going to get in the way of your system.
所以我不会妨碍你们的系统。

1002
00:46:31.730 --> 00:46:33.230
I hear all of that.
我全都听到了。

1003
00:46:33.390 --> 00:46:34.690
I just feel like pins.
我感觉就像针扎一样。

1004
00:46:34.970 --> 00:46:38.690
Like, I imagine she has seen Pam restock the supply shelf.
比如，我想象她一定见过帕姆整理补给架。

1005
00:46:38.970 --> 00:46:39.950
It's you, though.
但其实是你。

1006
00:46:40.550 --> 00:46:40.750
Yeah.
是啊。

1007
00:46:40.810 --> 00:46:41.050
Oh, right.
哦，对。

1008
00:46:41.130 --> 00:46:41.290
Sorry.
抱歉。

1009
00:46:41.330 --> 00:46:41.730
It's me.
是我。

1010
00:46:41.870 --> 00:46:42.350
It's not Erin.
不是艾琳。

1011
00:46:42.350 --> 00:46:42.810
Okay.
好吧。

1012
00:46:43.410 --> 00:46:44.870
I would probably be a busybody.
我大概会是个爱管闲事的人。

1013
00:46:45.570 --> 00:46:45.750
Hmm.
嗯。

1014
00:46:46.090 --> 00:46:46.390
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1015
00:46:46.870 --> 00:46:47.910
What are you out there?
你在外面是什么样的人？

1016
00:46:48.050 --> 00:46:49.590
Are you a busybody or a lazybones?
你是爱管闲事的人还是懒骨头？

1017
00:46:49.950 --> 00:46:52.870
I once had a coworker who called me Angela Two Cents.
我曾经有个同事叫我“安吉拉两分钱”。

1018
00:46:53.350 --> 00:46:54.190
Why is that?
为什么？

1019
00:46:54.330 --> 00:46:56.170
I had to put my two cents in everywhere.
因为我什么事都要插上一嘴。

1020
00:46:56.850 --> 00:46:57.750
How'd that go?
结果怎么样？

1021
00:46:58.330 --> 00:47:00.030
You just had a sidebar comment?
你只是在旁边评论一下吗？

1022
00:47:00.590 --> 00:47:03.570
I guess I had an opinion about how things were done.
我想是因为我对做事的方式有自己的看法。

1023
00:47:03.810 --> 00:47:05.450
That doesn't even seem like you.
那看起来一点都不像你。

1024
00:47:06.070 --> 00:47:08.250
Well, sit next to me in a cubicle all day,
好吧，跟我坐在同一个隔间里待上一整天，

1025
00:47:08.330 --> 00:47:10.170
and then you're going to be Angela Two Cents?
然后你就会变成“安吉拉两分钱”了？

1026
00:47:10.210 --> 00:47:11.870
Then I turn into Angela Two Cents.
那时我就变成了“安吉拉两分钱”。

1027
00:47:11.870 --> 00:47:12.450
Hmm.
嗯。

1028
00:47:12.850 --> 00:47:13.190
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1029
00:47:13.370 --> 00:47:18.010
This might be an interesting flavor to your mom detective's character.
这可能会为你妈妈侦探的角色增添一种有趣的特质。

1030
00:47:18.110 --> 00:47:18.530
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1031
00:47:18.730 --> 00:47:21.210
If I'm dropping everything and you're Angela Two Cents.
如果我放下一切，而你是“安吉拉两分钱”。

1032
00:47:21.390 --> 00:47:21.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1033
00:47:21.970 --> 00:47:23.090
I'm liking this.
我喜欢这个设定。

1034
00:47:23.390 --> 00:47:24.230
It's growing.
越来越有意思了。

1035
00:47:24.710 --> 00:47:28.650
Well, listen, in the kitchen, the taste test is continuing,
听着，在厨房里，试吃还在继续，

1036
00:47:30.010 --> 00:47:31.930
and energy is very high.
气氛非常高涨。

1037
00:47:32.290 --> 00:47:36.270
This scene is going to end with Kevin lifting you, Angela.
这一幕将以凯文抱起你结束，安吉拉。

1038
00:47:36.630 --> 00:47:38.010
Yeah, like I'm a barbell.
是啊，就像我是个杠铃一样。

1039
00:47:38.190 --> 00:47:39.430
That was scripted, right?
那是剧本里写的，对吧？

1040
00:47:39.610 --> 00:47:39.910
Yes.
是的。

1041
00:47:39.930 --> 00:47:40.950
That he's lifting you up.
他把你举起来。

1042
00:47:40.950 --> 00:47:41.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1043
00:47:41.430 --> 00:47:42.010
It is.
没错。

1044
00:47:42.410 --> 00:47:47.750
It was hilarious because I had to really make myself rigid, you know,
那太搞笑了，因为我必须让自己变得非常僵硬，你知道的，

1045
00:47:47.890 --> 00:47:49.950
like how you make your arms stiff at your side.
就像你把双臂紧贴在身体两侧那样。

1046
00:47:50.070 --> 00:47:50.290
Sure.
当然。

1047
00:47:50.410 --> 00:47:52.530
So that he could do that many repetitions.
这样他才能做那么多次重复动作。

1048
00:47:53.150 --> 00:47:53.910
Oh, uh-huh.
哦，嗯哼。

1049
00:47:54.150 --> 00:47:54.830
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1050
00:47:54.870 --> 00:47:56.290
Were you jumping a little bit?
你当时有稍微跳一下吗？

1051
00:47:56.330 --> 00:47:57.350
Were you helping him a little?
你刚才是不是稍微帮了他一把？

1052
00:47:57.530 --> 00:47:58.290
I was a little.
稍微帮了一点。

1053
00:47:58.590 --> 00:47:58.810
Okay.
好吧。

1054
00:47:58.810 --> 00:47:59.330
Can you tell?
你看得出来吗？

1055
00:47:59.910 --> 00:48:02.550
No, but I know the tricks of the trade.
看不出来，但我知道其中的门道。

1056
00:48:02.870 --> 00:48:03.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1057
00:48:03.290 --> 00:48:04.810
Well, because he had to do so many.
嗯，因为他得做那么多次。

1058
00:48:05.030 --> 00:48:09.690
And so to set me down all the way and get all, so I would just kind of spring down.
为了让我完全坐下并保持姿势，我得稍微弹跳着坐下去。

1059
00:48:09.890 --> 00:48:10.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1060
00:48:10.070 --> 00:48:12.850
I think it was a real workout for Brian.
我觉得这对布莱恩来说真的是种锻炼。

1061
00:48:14.870 --> 00:48:17.710
Well, Angela, we got a fan question from Shaley D.
安吉拉，我们收到了一位来自宾夕法尼亚州匹兹堡的粉丝谢莉·D的提问。

1062
00:48:17.970 --> 00:48:20.430
from Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania about this scene.
是关于这场戏的。

1063
00:48:21.090 --> 00:48:26.390
Shaley wanted to know, was everyone actually having shots of different types of espresso?
谢莉想知道，大家当时是真的在喝不同种类的浓缩咖啡吗？

1064
00:48:26.390 --> 00:48:27.930
What were you actually drinking?
你们当时到底在喝什么？

1065
00:48:29.050 --> 00:48:30.010
Shaley, no.
谢莉，不是的。

1066
00:48:30.250 --> 00:48:35.470
We were not actually drinking espresso because I think we'd all get sick if we had to drink it all day like that.
我们其实并没有喝浓缩咖啡，因为我觉得如果整天那样喝的话，我们都会生病的。

1067
00:48:35.650 --> 00:48:36.130
Thank goodness.
谢天谢地。

1068
00:48:36.470 --> 00:48:37.470
We were drinking water.
我们当时喝的是水。

1069
00:48:37.530 --> 00:48:40.390
And if you got close to my cup, mine had iced tea in it.
如果你凑近看我的杯子，我杯子里装的是冰茶。

1070
00:48:40.550 --> 00:48:42.510
