她翻看着桌上的杂志。

1391
01:01:32.430 --> 01:01:39.610
ESPN Magazine, Golf Digest, Baseball Digest, Sporting News, none of which she has any interest in.
《ESPN杂志》、《高尔夫文摘》、《棒球文摘》、《体育新闻》，这些她一点兴趣都没有。

1392
01:01:39.870 --> 01:01:42.890
She takes out her iPhone, tries to surf the web.
她拿出iPhone，试着上网。

1393
01:01:43.110 --> 01:01:45.990
The receptionist walks over from the outer office.
接待员从外面的办公室走了过来。

1394
01:01:46.510 --> 01:01:47.850
This made me laugh.
这段把我逗乐了。

1395
01:01:47.850 --> 01:01:49.810
The receptionist says to Pam,
接待员对帕姆说，

1396
01:01:50.170 --> 01:01:58.570
Our wireless password is ATHLETE, all lowercase except the A's, and then the L is a 1, and the H is a B, and the D is three ampersands.
我们的无线网密码是ATHLETE，除了A以外全部小写，L是数字1，H是字母B，D是三个和号。

1397
01:02:00.770 --> 01:02:04.810
Pam tries and then gives up, says, I'm okay, thanks.
帕姆试了一下然后放弃了，说，不用了，谢谢。

1398
01:02:08.980 --> 01:02:19.740
One of the things, Jenna, that when we started the podcast, when our offices were at Earwolf, every single time we went in, we'd have to log on to get internet.
珍娜，有一件事，当我们刚开始做播客，办公室还在Earwolf时，每次我们进去，都得登录才能连上网。

1399
01:02:19.740 --> 01:02:21.080
Oh, I hated that system.
哦，我讨厌那个系统。

1400
01:02:21.080 --> 01:02:23.960
And the password was so long and ridiculous.
那个密码又长又荒谬。

1401
01:02:24.460 --> 01:02:27.220
And when I read that, it just made me think of that.
当我读到那段时，它让我联想到了那个场景。

1402
01:02:27.420 --> 01:02:29.220
You know, you mentioned the receptioniSt.
你知道，你提到了那个前台接待员。

1403
01:02:29.480 --> 01:02:31.580
We got a fan question from Liv H.
我们收到了一位来自瑞典的粉丝Liv H.的提问，她说：

1404
01:02:31.760 --> 01:02:33.580
in Sweden who said,
她说，

1405
01:02:33.580 --> 01:02:40.320
I feel like if ATHLETE is a startup company and Jim doesn't even have a paycheck, how do they afford this receptionist?
我觉得如果ATHLETE是一家初创公司，而Jim甚至都没有工资拿，他们怎么请得起这个前台？

1406
01:02:40.600 --> 01:02:41.960
Like, what does he do?
他到底是干什么的？

1407
01:02:42.180 --> 01:02:43.240
Do they really need one?
他们真的需要前台吗？

1408
01:02:43.400 --> 01:02:44.980
It felt like a weird priority.
这感觉像是一个奇怪的优先事项。

1409
01:02:45.540 --> 01:02:49.440
You know, I wonder if this person is an intern.
我在想，这个人会不会是个实习生。

1410
01:02:50.920 --> 01:02:56.580
Like, a lot of startups will get, like, unpaid interns, and then they get, I don't know.
很多初创公司会招那种无薪实习生，然后他们能得到，我不知道，

1411
01:02:56.760 --> 01:02:58.400
Like, credit for school or something.
可能是学校的学分之类的东西。

1412
01:02:58.720 --> 01:03:01.060
Yeah, that made me wonder, because it's a good point.
是啊，这确实让我很好奇，因为这说得很有道理。

1413
01:03:01.460 --> 01:03:04.440
The receptionist was played by Rene Goubet.
前台接待员是由Rene Goubet扮演的。

1414
01:03:04.900 --> 01:03:09.660
He's a comedian, and he is currently working as a writer and co-executive producer of The Bear.
他是一位喜剧演员，目前担任《熊家餐馆》的编剧和联合执行制片人。

1415
01:03:09.840 --> 01:03:14.180
And before that, he was a co-executive producer of Justin Spitzer's show, Superstore.
在此之前，他是Justin Spitzer的剧集《爆笑超市》的联合执行制片人。

1416
01:03:14.180 --> 01:03:17.440
Well, Daryl's presentation has gone really well.
嗯，Daryl的演讲进行得非常顺利。

1417
01:03:17.660 --> 01:03:19.340
He's really turned things around.
他真的扭转了局面。

1418
01:03:19.460 --> 01:03:20.840
Everyone agrees.
大家都这么认为。

1419
01:03:21.280 --> 01:03:26.560
And sort of in the moment, he grabs a basketball that was there and—
就在那一刻，他顺手抓起了一个放在那里的篮球，然后——

1420
01:03:26.560 --> 01:03:28.000
A signed basketball.
一个签名篮球。

1421
01:03:28.000 --> 01:03:28.600
Yeah, yeah.
没错，没错。

1422
01:03:28.600 --> 01:03:30.700
Why would you shoot that in the first place?
你为什么要投那个球呢？

1423
01:03:30.700 --> 01:03:31.360
I don't know.
我不知道。

1424
01:03:31.520 --> 01:03:31.960
Go on.
继续说。

1425
01:03:31.960 --> 01:03:32.580
I know.
我知道。

1426
01:03:32.580 --> 01:03:40.940
And he tosses it to a basketball hoop, which is oddly placed near a light and a fish tank.
他把球投向了一个篮球框，那个篮筐奇怪地摆在灯和鱼缸旁边。

1427
01:03:41.340 --> 01:03:42.380
He misses.
他没投中。

1428
01:03:43.220 --> 01:03:47.640
It knocks the light into the fish tank and electrocutes all the fish.
球把灯撞进了鱼缸，电死了所有的鱼。

1429
01:03:47.960 --> 01:03:49.480
We got a fan mail flurry.
我们收到了大量的粉丝来信。

1430
01:03:49.740 --> 01:03:50.100
I bet.
我敢肯定。

1431
01:03:50.400 --> 01:03:52.320
People want to know, how did we do this?
大家想知道，我们是怎么拍出来的？

1432
01:03:52.600 --> 01:03:53.960
Did we have a safety meeting?
我们开过安全会议吗？

1433
01:03:54.320 --> 01:03:56.140
That spark looked so real.
那火花看起来太真实了。

1434
01:03:57.300 --> 01:04:02.940
How many takes was it to get the ball to hit the basket and the wall and the light and the tank?
为了让球击中篮筐、墙壁、灯和鱼缸，一共拍了多少次？

1435
01:04:03.300 --> 01:04:04.560
Were the fish fake?
那些鱼是假的吗？

1436
01:04:05.240 --> 01:04:07.200
Tell us everything about this scene.
告诉我们关于这个场景的一切吧。

1437
01:04:07.480 --> 01:04:10.080
Well, luckily, Matt Sohn had a lot to say about this scene.
幸运的是，Matt Sohn对这个场景有很多话要说。

1438
01:04:10.180 --> 01:04:10.780
Let's have a listen.
我们来听听看。

1439
01:04:11.520 --> 01:04:12.340
Let's see.
来看看吧。

1440
01:04:12.400 --> 01:04:19.480
The moment where Daryl accidentally electrocutes the fish was a fun gag.
Daryl意外电死鱼的那一刻是一个有趣的噱头。

1441
01:04:19.940 --> 01:04:28.820
We had rigged the lamp to fall into the fish tank and to pulsate, you know, to sell the electric shock.
我们安装了装置，让灯掉进鱼缸并产生脉冲，你知道，为了表现出触电的效果。

1442
01:04:28.820 --> 01:04:32.840
The floating dead fish really sold that moment.
漂浮的死鱼确实让那一刻显得很真实。

1443
01:04:33.200 --> 01:04:35.860
We had to work backwards on this bit.
我们必须倒着来设计这个桥段。

1444
01:04:36.560 --> 01:04:41.980
Phil Shea found the dead fish that we ultimately used.
Phil Shea找到了我们最终使用的死鱼。

1445
01:04:42.280 --> 01:04:47.500
You know, some were floating at the top of the tank and some were tied to monofilament.
有些鱼漂在鱼缸顶部，有些则用鱼线系着，

1446
01:04:47.500 --> 01:04:50.460
So they would float in the middle of the tank.
这样它们就能漂浮在鱼缸中间。

1447
01:04:50.780 --> 01:05:00.280
The challenge that we had was to find the live fish to match the dead ones that Phil had found, which we ultimately did, you know,
我们面临的挑战是找到与Phil找到的死鱼相匹配的活鱼，我们最终做到了，你知道，

1448
01:05:00.340 --> 01:05:07.300
so we could sell that there were live fish in the tank in other shots before Daryl throws the basketball.
这样我们就能在Daryl投篮前的其他镜头里展示鱼缸里是有活鱼的。

1449
01:05:07.300 --> 01:05:17.480
And I believe that Craig made that shot on the first take, but we did ultimately reset and did it a second time.
我相信Craig第一次投篮就中了，但我们最终还是重置并拍了第二次。

1450
01:05:17.480 --> 01:05:18.740
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1451
01:05:19.000 --> 01:05:19.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1452
01:05:19.560 --> 01:05:20.940
You can buy dead fish.
你可以买到死鱼。

1453
01:05:21.440 --> 01:05:24.020
Well, I had that question.
嗯，我当时就有这个疑问。

1454
01:05:24.260 --> 01:05:24.560
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1455
01:05:24.980 --> 01:05:26.440
I followed up with Matt.
我接着问了马特。

1456
01:05:26.720 --> 01:05:29.640
I said, do you mean real dead fish?
我说，你是说真的死鱼吗？

1457
01:05:30.020 --> 01:05:31.380
Or fake dead fish?
还是假的死鱼？

1458
01:05:31.380 --> 01:05:33.460
Here's what Matt had to say.
这是马特的回答。

1459
01:05:33.660 --> 01:05:33.860
Okay.
好的。

1460
01:05:34.780 --> 01:05:45.120
The fish that Phil Shea found were real dead fish, and they were sent to us frozen and packed.
菲尔·谢伊找到的鱼确实是死鱼，它们是冷冻包装后寄给我们的。

1461
01:05:45.380 --> 01:05:52.040
By about halfway through the shoot, most of the fish had thawed out and had started to smell.
拍摄进行到一半时，大多数鱼都已经解冻，开始散发出臭味了。

1462
01:05:52.040 --> 01:05:55.200
So it wasn't the most pleasant odor on set.
所以那并不是片场最令人愉快的味道。

1463
01:05:55.740 --> 01:05:57.400
That is so gross.
那太恶心了。

1464
01:05:57.640 --> 01:05:58.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1465
01:05:58.120 --> 01:06:03.160
I mean, were these dead fish that you could eat?
我是说，这些死鱼是可以吃的吗？

1466
01:06:03.320 --> 01:06:04.660
Are these fish edible?
这些鱼能吃吗？

1467
01:06:04.920 --> 01:06:06.460
I don't know what kind of fish they were.
我不知道它们是什么鱼。

1468
01:06:07.100 --> 01:06:08.860
Like your mallard story.
就像你那个野鸭的故事一样。

1469
01:06:09.240 --> 01:06:10.420
We may never know.
我们可能永远都不会知道了。

1470
01:06:10.520 --> 01:06:11.740
We're left with questions.
我们只能留下疑问。

1471
01:06:13.160 --> 01:06:19.940
Steve Burgess added that the light that fell into the tank was rigged so it could only fall in the tank.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯补充说，掉进鱼缸里的那盏灯是专门安装成只能掉进鱼缸里的。

1472
01:06:19.940 --> 01:06:26.200
And we added a safety to the light, kind of like the GFI in your kitchen, so that no one would get hurt when it sparked.
我们还给灯加了一个安全装置，就像你厨房里的漏电保护器一样，这样它冒火花时就不会有人受伤。

1473
01:06:26.200 --> 01:06:29.560
It was a grounded safety thing.
那是一个接地安全装置。

1474
01:06:29.960 --> 01:06:31.580
Probably not the technical term.
这大概不是专业术语。

1475
01:06:31.940 --> 01:06:32.760
Grounded safety thing.
接地安全装置。

1476
01:06:33.020 --> 01:06:33.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1477
01:06:33.620 --> 01:06:37.400
I loved all of that behind-the-scenes detail about that one stunt.
我很喜欢那个特技背后所有的幕后细节。

1478
01:06:37.680 --> 01:06:37.860
I know.
我知道。

1479
01:06:37.860 --> 01:06:39.320
That's amazing what all went into that.
为了那个镜头所做的一切真是太惊人了。

1480
01:06:39.560 --> 01:06:41.740
Well, Daryl now joins Pam at front reception.
好了，达里尔现在去前台和帕姆汇合了。

1481
01:06:41.780 --> 01:06:46.320
He's really down in the dumps because he just electrocuted everyone's fish.
他现在非常沮丧，因为他刚刚电死了所有人的鱼。

1482
01:06:46.320 --> 01:06:46.740
Why?
为什么？

1483
01:06:46.980 --> 01:06:47.720
Why are you laughing?
你笑什么？

1484
01:06:48.920 --> 01:06:50.000
Down in the dumps?
非常沮丧？

1485
01:06:50.080 --> 01:06:51.100
Is that a bad expression?
这个表达很糟糕吗？

1486
01:06:51.540 --> 01:06:54.060
I haven't known when to tell you.
我一直不知道该什么时候告诉你。

1487
01:06:54.240 --> 01:06:54.500
What?
什么？

1488
01:06:54.600 --> 01:06:55.120
What's on me?
我身上有什么东西吗？

1489
01:06:55.240 --> 01:06:55.920
Is something on me?
我身上沾了什么吗？

1490
01:06:55.980 --> 01:06:56.120
Some cheese.
一点奶酪。

1491
01:06:56.160 --> 01:06:57.640
Oh, I have a cheese on my boob.
哦，我胸口沾了块奶酪。

1492
01:06:58.280 --> 01:06:59.060
I have cheese.
我有奶酪。

1493
01:06:59.420 --> 01:07:00.580
You have a little cheese.
你沾了一点奶酪。

1494
01:07:00.620 --> 01:07:01.680
It's actually a cracker.
其实是块饼干。

1495
01:07:02.080 --> 01:07:02.640
It's a cracker.
是块饼干。

1496
01:07:03.120 --> 01:07:03.820
I ate it.
我把它吃了。

1497
01:07:04.000 --> 01:07:05.320
I ate it off my boob.
我直接从胸口把它吃了。

1498
01:07:05.540 --> 01:07:06.280
You know what?
你知道吗？

1499
01:07:06.280 --> 01:07:08.540
I remember you doing that early on the podcaSt.
我记得你在播客早期也做过这种事。

1500
01:07:08.840 --> 01:07:10.140
I remember you doing it.
我记得你做过。

1501
01:07:10.240 --> 01:07:11.440
You got a little thing.
你身上有个小东西。

1502
01:07:11.560 --> 01:07:12.240
Oh, it was me.
噢，是我弄的。

1503
01:07:12.240 --> 01:07:12.840
It was you.
是你弄的。

1504
01:07:12.960 --> 01:07:13.680
It wasn't me.
不是我。

1505
01:07:14.740 --> 01:07:15.100
Sorry.
抱歉。

1506
01:07:15.820 --> 01:07:20.900
I don't have any problem with eating stuff that's fallen on to you.
我不介意吃掉掉在你身上的东西。

1507
01:07:20.960 --> 01:07:21.620
I don't have a problem with that.
我对此没意见。

1508
01:07:21.620 --> 01:07:23.020
I had a little snack, guys.
伙计们，我刚才吃了点零食。

1509
01:07:23.220 --> 01:07:26.460
And I guess my dad used to say, well, you have a hitchhiker.
我想我爸以前常说，嗯，你身上有个搭便车的。

1510
01:07:26.940 --> 01:07:28.400
You had a hitchhiker, lady.
女士，你身上有个搭便车的。

1511
01:07:28.520 --> 01:07:28.840
I had a hitchhiker.
我身上有个搭便车的。

1512
01:07:29.220 --> 01:07:29.780
All right.
好吧。

1513
01:07:30.720 --> 01:07:37.760
Anyway, as I was saying, Daryl is down in the dumps, and Pam is trying to reassure him.
总之，正如我刚才所说，达里尔情绪低落，帕姆正试图安慰他。

1514
01:07:37.920 --> 01:07:38.680
She's like, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

1515
01:07:38.680 --> 01:07:41.940
At the end of the day, you have a great job where people love you.
归根结底，你有一份大家都很喜欢你的好工作。

1516
01:07:42.240 --> 01:07:42.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1517
01:07:42.880 --> 01:07:43.840
They start really bonding.
他们开始真正建立起感情了。

1518
01:07:44.040 --> 01:07:44.580
He's like, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1519
01:07:44.600 --> 01:07:46.000
I don't even think I want to live in Philly.
我觉得我甚至不想住在费城。

1520
01:07:46.200 --> 01:07:49.360
And Pam's like, yeah, it's not New York or London or Paris.
帕姆说，是啊，那又不是纽约、伦敦或巴黎。

1521
01:07:49.360 --> 01:07:50.440
Who needs Philly?
谁稀罕费城啊？

1522
01:07:51.080 --> 01:07:52.860
Jim comes out and says, guess what?
吉姆走出来说，你猜怎么着？

1523
01:07:53.060 --> 01:07:54.220
You got the job.
你得到那份工作了。

1524
01:07:55.200 --> 01:07:56.160
Daryl loves Philly.
达里尔爱死费城了。

1525
01:07:56.540 --> 01:07:58.540
All of a sudden, Daryl's super into Philly.
突然之间，达里尔对费城超级感兴趣。

1526
01:07:58.740 --> 01:07:59.800
Two, one, five or die.
215区，至死不渝。

1527
01:08:00.100 --> 01:08:00.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1528
01:08:01.080 --> 01:08:02.320
Pam has a talking head.
帕姆有个访谈镜头。

1529
01:08:02.500 --> 01:08:03.520
She says she's not upset.
她说她并不难过。

1530
01:08:03.660 --> 01:08:04.820
She's happy for Daryl.
她为达里尔感到高兴。

1531
01:08:05.280 --> 01:08:07.700
But she's a little disappointed they'll be losing him.
但她有点失望，因为他们要失去他了。

1532
01:08:08.120 --> 01:08:08.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1533
01:08:08.900 --> 01:08:12.260
Back at Dunder Mifflin, Erin decided to be a busybody.
回到邓德·米夫林，艾琳决定多管闲事。

1534
01:08:12.540 --> 01:08:16.940
She goes to unbox the pens, and everyone gives her grief about it.
她去拆开钢笔的包装，结果每个人都因此找她麻烦。

1535
01:08:17.100 --> 01:08:18.080
She gets all flustered.
她变得非常慌乱。

1536
01:08:18.160 --> 01:08:19.620
She puts the pens back in the box.
她把钢笔又放回了盒子里。

1537
01:08:19.620 --> 01:08:22.000
She is not gunning for Pam's job, okay?
她可不是在觊觎帕姆的工作，好吗？

1538
01:08:22.400 --> 01:08:25.600
But it's also, it's getting sweaty over in accounting.
但会计部那边也变得汗流浃背了。

1539
01:08:25.880 --> 01:08:27.280
It's getting real sweaty.
真的变得汗流浃背了。

1540
01:08:27.640 --> 01:08:30.360
Here is how this scene was described in the shooting draft.
以下是拍摄剧本中对这一场景的描述。

1541
01:08:30.360 --> 01:08:35.220
Interior office accounting area, Kevin is fidgety at his desk.
室内，办公室会计区，凯文在办公桌前坐立不安。

1542
01:08:35.400 --> 01:08:41.720
He has his suit jacket off, and he has gigantic armpit sweat stains, as well as sweat beads
他脱掉了西装外套，腋下有巨大的汗渍，额头上也挂着汗珠。

1543
01:08:41.720 --> 01:08:42.460
on his forehead.
我们能听到画外传来的敲击声。

1544
01:08:42.740 --> 01:08:45.380
We can hear an off-screen banging.
镜头向左平移，露出奥斯卡，他腋下也有巨大的汗渍。

1545
01:08:46.020 --> 01:08:50.780
Camera pans left to reveal Oscar, who also has huge armpit sweat stains.
镜头现在向右平移，露出安吉拉正向窗户那边探身，我们意识到。

1546
01:08:51.320 --> 01:08:57.260
Camera now pans right to reveal Angela leaning over towards the window, and we realize the
那敲击声是她为了打开窗户而拍打窗户的声音。

1547
01:08:57.260 --> 01:09:00.640
banging has been her smacking the window to try to open it.
她转向他们，我们看到她腋下也有巨大的汗渍。

1548
01:09:00.860 --> 01:09:05.380
She turns towards them, and we see that she, too, has enormous armpit stains.
所有关于腋下汗渍的描述都是大写加粗的。

1549
01:09:05.920 --> 01:09:09.480
Everything to do with the armpit stains is in all caps, and bold.
他们非常认真。

1550
01:09:09.700 --> 01:09:11.080
They were very serious.
他们非常认真。

1551
01:09:11.300 --> 01:09:13.580
They wanted us to have giant armpit stains.
他们想让我们腋下出现巨大的汗渍。

1552
01:09:14.020 --> 01:09:16.300
We got some fan mail about this scene, Angela.
安吉拉，我们收到了一些关于这场戏的粉丝来信。

1553
01:09:16.440 --> 01:09:17.240
People loved it.
大家都很喜欢。

1554
01:09:17.520 --> 01:09:18.040
Allie P.
来自爱达荷州的艾莉·P.

1555
01:09:18.300 --> 01:09:19.480
from Idaho said,
说，

1556
01:09:19.480 --> 01:09:24.140
I love how high-pitched everyone's voice gets, the deeper you get into the episode and
我喜欢大家的声音随着剧集深入变得越来越尖，

1557
01:09:24.140 --> 01:09:25.580
the more caffeine they've had.
而且咖啡因摄入得越多，声音就越尖。

1558
01:09:26.580 --> 01:09:27.880
And Levi D.
还有来自密歇根州的利维·D.

1559
01:09:28.100 --> 01:09:29.820
from Michigan said,
说，

1560
01:09:30.480 --> 01:09:33.740
Angela, how many takes did it take for you to get through that line?
安吉拉，你拍了多少条才说完那句台词？

1561
01:09:33.820 --> 01:09:35.780
I do not understand the point of windows.
我不明白窗户有什么意义。

1562
01:09:36.080 --> 01:09:39.720
The messy hair and sweaty pit reveal was so funny.
头发凌乱和腋下出汗的造型太搞笑了。

1563
01:09:41.200 --> 01:09:45.200
Well, Levi, the first thing is when they wrote this scene, and we did it at the table read,
嗯，利维，首先是当他们写这场戏时，我们在剧本围读会上，

1564
01:09:45.200 --> 01:09:49.660
none of us realized or remembered that that window is covered by blinds.
我们都没意识到或记起那扇窗户是被百叶窗挡住的。

1565
01:09:50.240 --> 01:09:54.740
So we sort of had to figure that out on the day that I would tuck in behind the blinds.
所以我们只能在拍摄当天临时想办法，让我躲在百叶窗后面。

1566
01:09:55.000 --> 01:09:57.840
And it was great because it naturally messed up my hair.
这很棒，因为它自然地弄乱了我的头发。

1567
01:09:58.660 --> 01:09:59.480
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1568
01:09:59.620 --> 01:10:02.260
We should tell people that's a completely fakie window.
我们应该告诉大家那是一扇完全假的窗户。

1569
01:10:02.480 --> 01:10:03.620
Yeah, that window goes nowhere.
对，那扇窗户根本通不到外面。

1570
01:10:04.120 --> 01:10:08.160
I actually love that the blinds were there because it gave me a bit of business to have to, like,
其实我挺喜欢有百叶窗的，因为它给了我一些动作戏，比如，

1571
01:10:08.580 --> 01:10:11.640
wrestle with as I come out from trying to open the window.
在我试图打开窗户出来时，不得不和它搏斗。

1572
01:10:12.460 --> 01:10:15.100
And we had so much fun in that scene.
我们在那场戏里玩得太开心了。

1573
01:10:15.720 --> 01:10:16.480
So much fun.
真的太开心了。

1574
01:10:16.620 --> 01:10:19.940
I think we only got to do a few takes of it, if I remember correctly.
如果我没记错的话，我们好像只拍了几条。

1575
01:10:20.300 --> 01:10:22.040
But we were having the best time.
但我们当时玩得最开心了。

1576
01:10:22.260 --> 01:10:28.220
Well, Angela, Matt Sohn talked about all that sweat and the Caffeine Corner storyline.
嗯，安吉拉，马特·索恩谈到了所有那些汗水和“咖啡因角落”的故事线。

1577
01:10:28.280 --> 01:10:29.320
Let's have a listen.
我们来听听看。

1578
01:10:30.140 --> 01:10:34.100
So Dan Graney was the writer of this episode.
丹·格雷尼是这一集的编剧。

1579
01:10:34.380 --> 01:10:42.220
We had had several conversations on how to best sell the escalation of the caffeine frenzy
我们讨论过很多次如何最好地呈现办公室里人们

1580
01:10:42.220 --> 01:10:44.100
of the people in the office.
咖啡因狂热的升级过程。

1581
01:10:44.100 --> 01:10:47.860
You know, it started with the cast slowly getting amped up.
你知道，一开始是演员们慢慢变得兴奋起来。

1582
01:10:48.100 --> 01:10:52.340
You know, they're all trying out the different espressos.
你知道，他们都在尝试不同的浓缩咖啡。

1583
01:10:52.540 --> 01:10:57.240
They decide that they're all going to have this challenge and try each flavor.
他们决定进行挑战，尝试每一种口味。

1584
01:10:57.240 --> 01:11:00.940
I think that also leads to Kevin picking up Angela.
我想这也导致了凯文抱起安吉拉那一幕。

1585
01:11:01.300 --> 01:11:03.220
I think that moment had us laughing.
我觉得那一刻让我们都笑了。

1586
01:11:03.600 --> 01:11:06.400
You know, there's also the moment of Stanley working away.
还有斯坦利努力工作的时刻。

1587
01:11:06.720 --> 01:11:09.800
He's very positive and upbeat and happy.
他非常积极、乐观且快乐。

1588
01:11:10.100 --> 01:11:14.520
You know, Kevin is rolling around on his chair in the office.
你知道，凯文在办公室里坐着椅子转来转去。

1589
01:11:14.780 --> 01:11:18.200
Then things start to go a little wrong.
然后事情开始有点不对劲了。

1590
01:11:18.600 --> 01:11:20.840
That's when everybody starts to get the sweats.
那就是每个人开始出汗的时候。

1591
01:11:20.840 --> 01:11:26.440
We had several different versions of the amount of sweat everybody had.
关于每个人出汗的程度，我们有几个不同的版本。

1592
01:11:26.580 --> 01:11:29.500
You know, we started light and then went heavier.
你知道，我们先从轻微的开始，然后加重。

1593
01:11:29.800 --> 01:11:36.620
You know, and I think it was obvious that the heavier, sweaty people made everybody laugh
你知道，我认为很明显，出汗更多的人让大家笑得

1594
01:11:36.620 --> 01:11:36.900
more.
更厉害。

1595
01:11:37.020 --> 01:11:38.720
So that's ultimately what we went for.
所以这最终成了我们的选择。

1596
01:11:38.720 --> 01:11:40.700
Do you remember that at all, Angela?
安吉拉，你还记得这些吗？

1597
01:11:40.860 --> 01:11:45.220
Do you remember them like spritzing you with sweat and then they were like more?
你记得他们给你喷汗水，然后说再多一点吗？

1598
01:11:45.700 --> 01:11:46.280
Oh, yeah.
哦，记得。

1599
01:11:46.500 --> 01:11:46.780
Oh, yeah.
哦，记得。

1600
01:11:47.020 --> 01:11:47.260
Yeah.
记得。

1601
01:11:47.320 --> 01:11:52.980
They also purposely had me in a long sleeve shirt so I could show more sweat because normally
他们还特意让我穿长袖衬衫，这样我能多出点汗，因为平时

1602
01:11:52.980 --> 01:11:54.540
I wear like a little blouse.
我穿的都是那种小衬衫。

1603
01:11:54.700 --> 01:11:54.880
Sure.
确实。

1604
01:11:55.300 --> 01:11:59.100
And hair and makeup were standing just right off camera and they had the spray bottles
发型和化妆师就站在镜头外，手里拿着喷雾瓶，

1605
01:11:59.100 --> 01:12:02.960
and they would come in and squirt us like to get us more damp.
他们会走过来往我们身上喷水，让我们看起来更湿润。

1606
01:12:02.960 --> 01:12:04.340
What did you do at work today?
你今天上班都干了些什么？

1607
01:12:04.620 --> 01:12:06.880
I got squirted in my armpits.
我被人往腋下喷水了。

1608
01:12:07.040 --> 01:12:07.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1609
01:12:07.480 --> 01:12:08.320
With water bottles.
用喷水瓶喷的。

1610
01:12:08.760 --> 01:12:12.500
And then I watched dead fish get thawed out.
然后我还看着死鱼被解冻。

1611
01:12:13.360 --> 01:12:14.920
What is your job?
你是做什么工作的？

1612
01:12:16.280 --> 01:12:22.000
Well, now that they have all this energy, Oscar suggests that they move the copier into the
好吧，既然他们现在精力充沛，奥斯卡建议他们把复印机搬到

1613
01:12:22.000 --> 01:12:23.580
annex like they've always wanted to.
附楼去，就像他们一直想做的那样。

1614
01:12:23.800 --> 01:12:24.220
Yes.
没错。

1615
01:12:24.320 --> 01:12:27.020
I loved it when Kevin was like, goodbye, noise.
凯文说“再见，噪音”的时候，我真是太喜欢了。

1616
01:12:28.580 --> 01:12:30.860
Isn't there already a copier in the annex?
附楼里不是已经有一台复印机了吗？

1617
01:12:31.440 --> 01:12:35.180
There is, but they just needed a project, lady.
是有，但他们只是需要找点事做，女士。

1618
01:12:35.380 --> 01:12:36.400
I guess so.
我想也是。

1619
01:12:36.800 --> 01:12:41.780
Well, when they start moving this copier, it rips up the carpet and it reveals beautiful
好吧，当他们开始搬这台复印机时，地毯被扯开了，露出了漂亮的

1620
01:12:41.780 --> 01:12:44.980
hardwood floors, which Oscar knew were there all along.
硬木地板，而奥斯卡一直都知道下面有地板。

1621
01:12:45.540 --> 01:12:47.180
Oscar's so happy about it.
奥斯卡对此感到非常高兴。

1622
01:12:47.700 --> 01:12:49.880
Meredith yells for them to rip up all the carpet.
梅雷迪思大喊着让他们把所有的地毯都扯掉。

1623
01:12:50.180 --> 01:12:50.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1624
01:12:50.600 --> 01:12:52.480
You need to see all the hardwood floors.
你需要看看所有的硬木地板。

1625
01:12:52.860 --> 01:12:55.600
Angela, I have to ask, what do you remember about this scene?
安吉拉，我得问问，关于这一幕你还记得什么？

1626
01:12:55.680 --> 01:12:59.440
You aren't really physically ripping up the carpet, but what do you remember from shooting
你并不是真的在物理上扯掉地毯，但拍摄这一幕时

1627
01:12:59.440 --> 01:12:59.860
this?
你记得什么？

1628
01:12:59.860 --> 01:13:02.160
I mean, everybody had a really good time.
我是说，每个人都玩得很开心。

1629
01:13:02.460 --> 01:13:03.720
I don't know what it is.
我不知道为什么。

1630
01:13:04.000 --> 01:13:09.000
When you're given permission to like rip something or pull something apart, I think everybody is
当你被允许去撕扯或拆解什么东西时，我想每个人都会觉得，

1631
01:13:09.000 --> 01:13:10.120
like, I'm here for it.
我乐意效劳。

1632
01:13:10.380 --> 01:13:12.180
Get out some of your aggressions.
发泄一下你的情绪。

1633
01:13:12.440 --> 01:13:15.020
I just like that everything was giving Angela a headache.
我只是喜欢那种所有事情都让安吉拉头疼的感觉。

1634
01:13:15.260 --> 01:13:15.660
Yes.
没错。

1635
01:13:15.740 --> 01:13:17.280
Well, she gets her headaches, you know.
嗯，你知道的，她总是会头疼。

1636
01:13:17.380 --> 01:13:17.960
She does.
确实。

1637
01:13:18.260 --> 01:13:20.520
We got a fan question from Jessica N.
我们收到了来自纽约州罗切斯特市杰西卡·N的一位粉丝提问，

1638
01:13:20.600 --> 01:13:22.940
in Rochester, New York, who said, how did they get the wooden
她问，他们是怎么在办公室的地毯下弄出木质

1639
01:13:22.940 --> 01:13:25.020
flooring underneath the carpet in the office?
地板的？

1640
01:13:25.020 --> 01:13:29.660
Did they set it on top of real gray carpet and then add another layer of carpet?
他们是把它铺在真正的灰色地毯上，然后又加了一层地毯吗？

1641
01:13:30.060 --> 01:13:32.220
Whatever they did, I'm sure it was a lot of work.
不管他们是怎么做的，我敢肯定那一定费了很大功夫。

1642
01:13:32.920 --> 01:13:35.160
Steve Burgess said it was a lot of work.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说那确实费了很大功夫。

1643
01:13:35.260 --> 01:13:35.800
I bet.
我敢肯定。

1644
01:13:36.180 --> 01:13:38.780
That basically, we picked the areas where we would see the flooring.
基本上，我们挑选了能看到地板的区域。

1645
01:13:38.920 --> 01:13:39.800
We ripped up the carpet.
我们扯掉了地毯。

1646
01:13:39.820 --> 01:13:40.740
We put down the flooring.
我们铺上了地板。

1647
01:13:40.740 --> 01:13:42.180
We put carpet back on top of it.
我们又在上面铺回了地毯。

1648
01:13:42.240 --> 01:13:43.120
We ripped up the carpet.
我们扯掉了地毯。

1649
01:13:43.460 --> 01:13:48.320
But in the end, we had to pull up all the carpet and replace it for the next episode.
但最后，我们不得不把所有的地毯都掀起来，并在下一集之前换上新的。

1650
01:13:48.740 --> 01:13:52.860
Matt said they had a carpet installation team standing by to fix it as soon as we wrapped.
马特说，他们安排了地毯安装团队随时待命，一旦我们收工就立刻修复。

1651
01:13:53.500 --> 01:13:57.540
And Steve Burgess reminded me that this is not the first time we've had to replace a bunch
史蒂夫·伯吉斯提醒我，这已经不是我们第一次需要更换一大片

1652
01:13:57.540 --> 01:13:57.960
of carpet.
地毯了。

1653
01:13:58.600 --> 01:14:02.640
He said, remember when Michael proposed to Holly and it set off all the sprinklers?
他说，还记得迈克尔向霍莉求婚，结果触发了所有喷淋装置那次吗？

1654
01:14:03.100 --> 01:14:06.640
He said we had to replace all of the carpet after that episode as well.
他说那次事件之后，我们也必须更换所有的地毯。

1655
01:14:06.640 --> 01:14:10.500
And one square when Kevin spills the chili.
还有凯文洒了辣椒酱的那一小块。

1656
01:14:11.400 --> 01:14:12.120
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1657
01:14:12.480 --> 01:14:13.200
That's true.
那是真的。

1658
01:14:13.760 --> 01:14:20.280
I think we had to replace the carpet in Michael's office when Packer put the poop in there, too.
我想帕克在迈克尔办公室里放了那坨东西的时候，我们也得换地毯。

1659
01:14:20.480 --> 01:14:21.020
Oh, right.
哦，没错。

1660
01:14:21.780 --> 01:14:22.260
Anyway.
总之。

1661
01:14:22.840 --> 01:14:23.820
We were busy.
我们当时很忙。

1662
01:14:23.940 --> 01:14:25.220
We kept the carpet people busy.
我们让铺地毯的人忙得团团转。

1663
01:14:25.320 --> 01:14:25.680
We did.
确实。

1664
01:14:26.020 --> 01:14:29.740
Well, after they rip up all the carpet, everyone's going to try to leave simultaneously.
好吧，等他们把地毯全拆了，大家肯定会想同时离开。

1665
01:14:31.400 --> 01:14:33.700
And it doesn't go well in the parking lot.
停车场里肯定会乱成一团。

1666
01:14:33.860 --> 01:14:35.960
This scene really cracks me up.
这一幕真的让我笑喷了。

1667
01:14:35.960 --> 01:14:39.240
I went to the shooting draft, and this is how it was described.
我查了拍摄剧本，上面是这样描述的。

1668
01:14:39.680 --> 01:14:41.760
Exterior parking lot moments later.
外景，停车场，片刻之后。

1669
01:14:41.960 --> 01:14:46.680
From the upstairs window, we see people in their cars caught in a huge traffic snarl.
从楼上的窗户看去，我们看到人们的车被困在巨大的交通堵塞中。

1670
01:14:46.860 --> 01:14:51.720
It's a cacophony of honking horns with a few people leaning out their windows and yelling.
到处是刺耳的喇叭声，还有几个人探出车窗大喊大叫。

1671
01:14:52.240 --> 01:14:54.500
Others gunning it, then slamming on their brakes.
其他人猛踩油门，然后又猛踩刹车。

1672
01:14:54.740 --> 01:14:57.920
Someone dangerously tries to weave between cars, et cetera.
有人危险地试图在车流中穿插，诸如此类。

1673
01:14:58.340 --> 01:15:00.220
So there was no dialogue scripted for us.
所以我们当时没有预设台词。

1674
01:15:00.340 --> 01:15:04.360
Everything that you see in the parking lot or heard, that was all improvised in the moment.
你在停车场看到或听到的一切，都是当时即兴发挥的。

1675
01:15:04.700 --> 01:15:05.420
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

1676
01:15:05.420 --> 01:15:05.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1677
01:15:06.220 --> 01:15:06.880
Very good.
非常好。

1678
01:15:07.140 --> 01:15:07.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1679
01:15:07.700 --> 01:15:12.060
And obviously, all the carve movements were completely planned.
显然，所有的车辆移动都是完全规划好的。

1680
01:15:12.120 --> 01:15:17.240
Everyone knew exactly where they were going in their car, so there was no actual real fender
每个人都知道自己的车该往哪开，所以没有发生任何真正的

1681
01:15:17.240 --> 01:15:17.580
bender.
剐蹭。

1682
01:15:18.900 --> 01:15:22.520
So movement choreographed, lines improvised.
所以动作是编排好的，台词是即兴的。

1683
01:15:22.700 --> 01:15:23.140
Exactly.
没错。

1684
01:15:23.520 --> 01:15:26.140
Well, now Daryl and Pam are back in the car.
好了，现在达里尔和帕姆回到了车里。

1685
01:15:26.300 --> 01:15:27.420
They're heading back to Scranton.
他们正准备回斯克兰顿。

1686
01:15:27.560 --> 01:15:28.860
Daryl is so pumped.
达里尔非常兴奋。

1687
01:15:29.040 --> 01:15:29.680
So excited.
特别激动。

1688
01:15:29.820 --> 01:15:30.720
He starts singing.
他开始唱歌。

1689
01:15:31.160 --> 01:15:33.220
